/* =====================================================================
   WA v258 the Fundraising meeting's follow-through (15/10/26)
   =====================================================================
   Steel, in the 15/10/26 Fundraising meeting with Amanda (the lead), Alyx and Alexis (new): "I'll make those improvements
   tonight". Amanda opened Open decisions on Home and landed on the executive view with everyone's tasks; the Grants workstream
   (14 open) cluttered the Fundraising page; "Fundraising homepage should just say the requests, so whenever a department asks
   for something at another meeting"; Alexis got stuck on the task check pop-up (wave213; the explainer and the answered count
   live in parts213).
   - Home chips (renderMyPage, decorated after each render; the clicks are taken in the capture phase so the older chip
     handlers stand aside): my open tasks scrolls to My tasks and lights it; team tasks opens the person's team page; open
     decisions, for anyone who is not an admin or on the executive team, counts their team's open decisions and opens the team
     page at its decisions (or says plainly that there are none); admins and the executive team keep the executive view
     (#overview). Who may open the Dashboard is unchanged. incoming requests lands on the team page's requests.
   - Team pages: when a team has open requests (asked of it by another team, in a meeting or through Requests), they show at
     the top, above the page's tabs (#w258req); a click opens the request in place (wave123's sheet).
   - Grants gets its own page (#grants, in the Fundraising row of the menu; WA_TEAMS ADOPT in wave116): the Grants workstream's
     tasks on the standard board (tick, open, the bank in the drawer), Add a grants task (filed under fundraising / Grants),
     Overseen by the grants lead (Suhaib), and the Fundraising app's grants pipeline. On the Fundraising team page the Grants
     group is a pointer, and the page's totals leave grants out (window.w116TasksFor, wrapped). No new team code: grants stay
     dept_tasks.department fundraising, subsection Grants. Seen by whoever can see Fundraising (wa40Allowed, wrapped).
   ===================================================================== */
(function () {
